"""cube_fx_common.h's fx_step: a rate per 23 ms frame scaled to the frame's real length. It truncated, so any
rate x dt under 23 came out 0 - a slow spin stood still and a peak-hold decay never fell above 43 fps. Cube Frame's
spin slider one step off centre is a rate of 1: at 8 ms frames it has to turn the cube, where the old helper left
the picture exactly as with the slider centred. Needs a built engine (python build.py --native-only).
Run with  python tests/test_fx_step.py  (or pytest)."""
